course: dictionary
lesson: 10253
title: One word, many meanings: ton
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. «Bracken Cave in Texas has millions of bats... and they eat tons of insects every night.» Here tons of means a huge amount, because the sentence is about how much the bats eat, not how heavy anything is.
explain: When ton is a unit of weight, the sentence will mention weight, kilograms or pounds. «A ton is about a thousand kilograms, as heavy as a small car.» That tells you a ton is very heavy. In science and maths we usually use the tonne, which is also 1,000 kilograms.
explain: In cricket, a ton is a score of a hundred runs. In everyday talk, «it weighs a ton» means it is too heavy. A school bag weighs perhaps five kilograms, far less than a ton, so the words are an exaggeration. Check your meaning by swapping in «a lot of» or «very heavy». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Ton is a noun: a ton, tons.
fact: A ton is a large unit of weight: a long ton is 2,240 pounds in the UK, and a short ton is 2,000 pounds in the US.
fact: A tonne, or metric ton, is 1,000 kilograms, and it is the one used in science and maths.
fact: «Tons of» means a lot of something, as in «I've got tons of homework.»
fact: In UK slang, a ton is a hundred: a century in cricket, or «do a ton», which means driving at 100 miles an hour.
exercise: «Bracken Cave in Texas has millions of bats... and they eat tons of insects every night.» What does tons of mean here? | Exactly two | *A lot of | A small amount | Weighing in pounds
exercise: «A 2.5-tonne elephant» weighs how many kilograms? | 250 kg | *2,500 kg | 2.5 kg | 25 kg
exercise: Priya's school bag is heavy, so she says «it weighs a ton». What does she mean? | *It is too heavy | It is made of metal | It weighs exactly one tonne | It weighs one kilogram
test: In cricket, what does «scoring a ton» mean? | Losing the match | Scoring 10 runs | *Scoring a hundred runs | Running very fast
test: How many kilograms is one tonne? | *1,000 | 10,000 | 100 | 2,240
exam: Which statement about a long ton used in the UK is correct? | *It is 2,240 pounds | It is a hundred runs in cricket | It is 2,000 pounds | It is 1,000 kilograms
